[break] the-sighup-after-a-hang-up-ends-the-process
rule: The SIGHUP that follows a hang-up already taken as SIGHUP's end is that same end, not a second signal that ends the process part-way.
file: crates/cortex-term/src/sys/unix.rs
in: on_ending
find: if signal == libc::SIGHUP && super::hung_up_already(129) {
replace: if false {
