[break] leaving-puts-back-the-default-handlers
rule: While signals are handed to the program, leaving the terminal keeps the handlers of the signals that end it until signal_ended: one that comes while the program ends is handed over, not the default action's.
file: crates/cortex-term/src/sys/unix.rs
in: leave
find: if keep && ENDING.contains(&signal) && !(guarding && is_interrupt(signal)) {
replace: if false && keep && ENDING.contains(&signal) && !(guarding && is_interrupt(signal)) {
packages: cortex-tui
caught-by:
    cortex-tui::it signals::sys_closing_the_terminal_ends_as_sighup

[break] no-watchdog
rule: A signal handed to the program sets the watchdog, which ends the process if the program has not ended itself within 3 s.
file: crates/cortex-term/src/sys/unix.rs
in: on_ending
find: unsafe { libc::alarm(WATCHDOG_SECONDS) };
replace: let _ = WATCHDOG_SECONDS;
caught-by:
    cortex-term::it handoff::sys_a_signal_handed_over_sets_the_watchdog_and_erases_the_whole_region

[break] a-second-signal-is-handed-over-too
rule: A second signal, while the program ends what the first asked, ends the process at once by its own action.
file: crates/cortex-term/src/sys/mod.rs
in: hand_over
find: .compare_exchange(0, code, Ordering::SeqCst, Ordering::SeqCst)
replace: .swap(code, Ordering::SeqCst).checked_add(0).ok_or(())
caught-by:
    cortex-term::it handoff::sys_a_second_signal_ends_the_process_at_once

[break] the-restore-erases-from-the-cursor-down
rule: The emergency restore moves up to the live region's first row before it erases, so none of the region stays on the screen.
