[break] the-viewer-is-left-after-the-region-is-erased
rule: The application leaves the viewer's alternate screen before the presenter erases the live region, so the main screen is left as a plain quit leaves it.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app.rs
in: run_with
find: terminal.alternate(false)?;
replace: let _ = ();
caught-by:
    cortex-tui::it signals::sys_quitting_from_the_viewer_leaves_the_main_screen_clean

[break] the-core-is-not-waited-for
rule: The binary waits for the core's end (its last records on disk) before it exits: after a signal, the stopped turn's records are written by that end.
file: crates/cortex-cli/src/interactive.rs
in: CoreThread::end
find: let deadline = end_deadline(began, within, signalled);
replace: let deadline = began;
caught-by:
    cortex-cli::system tui::sys_a_signal_ends_the_application_gracefully_with_its_code

[break] a-signal-does-not-shorten-the-cores-end
rule: After a signal the core is given at most 1.5 s, from the signal, so the program ends before its watchdog does.
file: crates/cortex-cli/src/interactive.rs
in: end_deadline
find: signalled.map_or(deadline, |at| deadline.min(at + SIGNAL_END))
replace: signalled.map_or(deadline, |_| deadline)
caught-by:
    interactive::tests::the_cores_end_is_cut_short_by_a_signal

[break] the-log-flush-waits-for-ever
rule: The log's flush at the end waits at most its limit for a writer stuck on its disk.
file: crates/cortex-base/src/log/file.rs
in: FileSink::flush_within
find: wait.recv_timeout(left)
replace: Ok::<(), std::sync::mpsc::RecvTimeoutError>(wait.recv().unwrap_or(()))
caught-by:
    log::tests::a_flush_within_a_limit_gives_up_on_a_stuck_writer

[break] the-terminal-is-taken-back-after-a-signal
